38.030Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\frontend","sessionId":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"frontend/diagnosis"}
{"parentUuid":"1f929d8c-d594-479c-90a6-43e7717bd0bb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"dc600319-4f96-4ead-b3c9-3fbae41c33ba","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016TfrgzrPWK6dZGTeKrTi26","type":"tool_result","content":"\u001b[32m✓ built in 895ms\u001b[39m","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b802d752-b412-45aa-b1eb-56ce015b0b2d","timestamp":"2026-11-08T05:07:44.782Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"\u001b[32m✓ built in 895ms\u001b[39m","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\docs\\STATUS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":114,"newStart":1,"newLines":114,"lines":["-# Status — the shared task board","-","-**This is the one place work is claimed.** Read it at the start of every","-session. Claim before you write code. Release when you stop.","-","-There is no task framework to install — `gh` isn't on these machines and","-four people on three different AI harnesses have exactly one medium in","-common, which is this repo. So the board is a file, and the protocol below","-is what makes it work.","-","-Last updated: **2026-11-07**","-","----","-","-## How to claim (all of it)","-","-1. **`git pull`** — then put your name on the line you want, in **In flight**.","-2. **Commit just this file and push immediately.** Don't bundle the claim","-   with your work; the claim is worthless if it lands an hour later.","-   ```bash","-   git pull && git add docs/STATUS.md && git commit -m \"claim: <task>\" && git push","-   ```","-3. **If the push is rejected**, someone claimed something while you typed.","-   `git pull --rebase`, check your task is still free, push again.","-4. **When you stop** — done, blocked, or bored — move the line to **Done** or","-   back to **Open**, with one line on where you left it. A task parked","-   silently is the same as a task nobody did.","-","-If two of you end up on the same line anyway, that's a conflict in one","-markdown row. Keep both names, talk, move on.","-","-**Your task isn't on the board?** Most won't be. Add the line and claim it","-in the same push — that *is* the claim. Don't go looking for permission.","-","-**When not to claim.** Claiming costs a push, so it has to buy something.","-Skip it for anything another person could not plausibly start at the same","-time: reading code, answering a question, a typo, a one-line fix, anything","-under ~10 minutes. Claim when you're about to **create a file, change a","-shared one, or work somewhere for a while** — that's when collisions happen.","-A board full of \"fixed a typo\" is a board nobody reads.","-","----","-","-## In flight — claimed, don't touch","-","-| Who | Track | Branch | Task | Blocked on |","-|---|---|---|---|---|","-| Jeremy | discovery | `main` | FUS discovery pipeline — scripted end to end. See `DISCOVERY_SPEC.md` | A live backend behind `runDemoPipeline` |","-| Jeremy | frontend | `main` | Motus dashboard — overview landed, 15 views still placeholders | Supabase keys |","-| Neo | pipeline | `cursor/pipeline-graph-ui` | Drug pipeline — BBB + patient filter scored over 3,791 compounds | — |","-| Neo | facecheck | `cursor/facial-als-validation` | FaceCheck MediaPipe prototype | `FACECHECK_SPEC.md` §2 gaps |","-| Levi | speech | `Master-UI-Neo-Face-Integration` | Speech + diagnostic test apps | No spec in `docs/` yet |","-| Henri | repo | `main` | Cleanup, specs, this board | — |","-","-> Names are from git history. Fix them if they're wrong.","-","-## Open — unclaimed, grab one","-","-Ordered roughly by what hurts most if it's still open on Sunday morning.","-","-| Track | Task | Why it matters |","-|---|---|---|","-| **decision** | **Pick the product: discovery pipeline or Motus.** Both ship on `main`, in one sidebar, sharing nothing else | 90 seconds, one argument. Everything below depends on this |","-| **decision** | **Pick the name.** Code says *Addo Labs*, landing page says *motus* | A judge sees both in one scroll |","-| discovery | Wire the graveyard's `never_arrived` bucket in as the FUS candidate pool | It already exists in `data/pipeline.json` and is exactly the right set — `DISCOVERY_SPEC.md` §1 |","-| discovery | Real citations for the Sunnybrook MRgFUS claim; be precise about human vs proposed | The whole pitch rests on it, and someone will ask |","-| pipeline | Port the Python onto a branch cut from `main` (leave `data/*.json` and `artifacts/` behind) | `main` has no pipeline code today |","-| speech | Write `docs/SPEECH_SPEC.md` | The only track with no spec — nobody else can pick it up |","-| frontend | Decide demo mode: signed-in or sample data | Sample works today with no keys |","-| facecheck | Decide: own page, or a tab in the app | `FACECHECK_SPEC.md` §7 |","-| discovery | A real backend behind `runDemoPipeline` — stretch | The seam is clean; don't collapse it under time pressure |","-","-## Done","-","-- **2026-11-08** · Jeremy · Landing reworked: neuron lies horizontally across","-  the top (soma right, axon running left), name bottom-left; each action","-  potential runs to the terminals and an amber glow carries on down to light","-  the wordmark. Discovery pipeline now advances one stage per click, Gradient","-  ASCII background (React Bits, patched for StrictMode) replaces the dither.","-- **2026-11-07** · Henri · Repo cleanup: `app/` and `web/` deleted, contract","-  extracted to `contract/`, `.gitignore` rewritten (`.env` was exposed),","-  `.workspace/` added, CI deleted — run `npm test --prefix contract` yourself.","-- **2026-11-07** · Henri · `DISCOVERY_SPEC.md` written from Jeremy's pitch.","-- **2026-11-07** · Jeremy · Discovery pipeline UI + Motus dashboard merged","-  (PRs #1, #2).","-","----","-","-## If main gives you a `tsconfig.tsbuildinfo` conflict — read this first","-","-**Jeremy, this is the one you're hitting.** `frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo`","-is TypeScript's incremental build cache. It was committed by mistake, it","-rewrites itself on every single build, so it conflicted constantly. `main`","-untracked it on 2026-11-07 and it's gitignored now.","-","-Your branch has it modified, main deleted it → modify/delete conflict.","-Accept the deletion; it regenerates on your next build and will never come","-back:","-","-```bash","-git rm --cached frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo","-git commit --no-edit","-```","-","-One time only. Sorry — that one's on Henri, and it was the only file under","-`frontend/` that main touched.","-","-## Heads-up if you merge main","-","-`main` deleted `app/` on 2026-11-07, so branches that built there get","-modify/delete conflicts (measured: 11 on `cursor/pipeline-graph-ui`, 19 on","-`frontend/kg-and-provenance`). `Master-UI-Neo-Face-Integration` and","-`codex/diagnostic-tests` share **no common ancestor** with main and can't be","-merged without `--allow-unrelated-histories`. Your branch, your call.","+# Status — the shared task board\r","+\r","+**This is the one place work is claimed.** Read it at the start of every\r","+session. Claim before you write code. Release when you stop.\r","+\r","+There is no task framework to install — `gh` isn't on these machines and\r","+four people on three different AI harnesses have exactly one medium in\r","+common, which is this repo. So the board is a file, and the protocol below\r","+is what makes it work.\r","+\r","+Last updated: **2026-11-07**\r","+\r","+---\r","+\r","+## How to claim (all of it)\r","+\r","+1. **`git pull`** — then put your name on the line you want, in **In flight**.\r","+2. **Commit just this file and push immediately.** Don't bundle the claim\r","+   with your work; the claim is worthless if it lands an hour later.\r","+   ```bash\r","+   git pull && git add docs/STATUS.md && git commit -m \"claim: <task>\" && git push\r","+   ```\r","+3. **If the push is rejected**, someone claimed something while you typed.\r","+   `git pull --rebase`, check your task is still free, push again.\r","+4. **When you stop** — done, blocked, or bored — move the line to **Done** or\r","+   back to **Open**, with one line on where you left it. A task parked\r","+   silently is the same as a task nobody did.\r","+\r","+If two of you end up on the same line anyway, that's a conflict in one\r","+markdown row. Keep both names, talk, move on.\r","+\r","+**Your task isn't on the board?** Most won't be. Add the line and claim it\r","+in the same push — that *is* the claim. Don't go looking for permission.\r","+\r","+**When not to claim.** Claiming costs a push, so it has to buy something.\r","+Skip it for anything another person could not plausibly start at the same\r","+time: reading code, answering a question, a typo, a one-line fix, anything\r","+under ~10 minutes. Claim when you're about to **create a file, change a\r","+shared one, or work somewhere for a while** — that's when collisions happen.\r","+A board full of \"fixed a typo\" is a board nobody reads.\r","+\r","+---\r","+\r","+## In flight — claimed, don't touch\r","+\r","+| Who | Track | Branch | Task | Blocked on |\r","+|---|---|---|---|---|\r","+| Jeremy | discovery | `main` | FUS discovery pipeline — scripted end to end. See `DISCOVERY_SPEC.md` | A live backend behind `runDemoPipeline` |\r","+| Jeremy | frontend | `main` | Motus dashboard — overview landed, 15 views still placeholders | Supabase keys |\r","+| Neo | pipeline | `cursor/pipeline-graph-ui` | Drug pipeline — BBB + patient filter scored over 3,791 compounds | — |\r","+| Neo | facecheck | `cursor/facial-als-validation` | FaceCheck MediaPipe prototype | `FACECHECK_SPEC.md` §2 gaps |\r","+| Levi | speech | `Master-UI-Neo-Face-Integration` | Speech + diagnostic test apps | No spec in `docs/` yet |\r","+| Henri | repo | `main` | Cleanup, specs, this board | — |\r","+\r","+> Names are from git history. Fix them if they're wrong.\r","+\r","+## Open — unclaimed, grab one\r","+\r","+Ordered roughly by what hurts most if it's still open on Sunday morning.\r","+\r","+| Track | Task | Why it matters |\r","+|---|---|---|\r","+| **decision** | **Pick the product: discovery pipeline or Motus.** Both ship on `main`, in one sidebar, sharing nothing else | 90 seconds, one argument. Everything below depends on this |\r","+| **decision** | **Pick the name.** Code says *Addo Labs*, landing page says *motus* | A judge sees both in one scroll |\r","+| discovery | Wire the graveyard's `never_arrived` bucket in as the FUS candidate pool | It already exists in `data/pipeline.json` and is exactly the right set — `DISCOVERY_SPEC.md` §1 |\r","+| discovery | Real citations for the Sunnybrook MRgFUS claim; be precise about human vs proposed | The whole pitch rests on it, and someone will ask |\r","+| pipeline | Port the Python onto a branch cut from `main` (leave `data/*.json` and `artifacts/` behind) | `main` has no pipeline code today |\r","+| speech | Write `docs/SPEECH_SPEC.md` | The only track with no spec — nobody else can pick it up |\r","+| frontend | Decide demo mode: signed-in or sample data | Sample works today with no keys |\r","+| facecheck | Decide: own page, or a tab in the app | `FACECHECK_SPEC.md` §7 |\r","+| discovery | A real backend behind `runDemoPipeline` — stretch | The seam is clean; don't collapse it under time pressure |\r","+\r","+## Done\r","+\r","+- **2026-11-08** · Jeremy · Landing reworked: neuron lies horizontally, tilted\r","+  slightly (soma left, axon sloping down to the right), name bottom-right; each\r","+  action potential runs to the far terminals and an amber glow carries on down\r","+  to light the wordmark. Discovery pipeline now advances one stage per click, Gradient\r","+  ASCII background (React Bits, patched for StrictMode) replaces the dither.\r","+- **2026-11-07** · Henri · Repo cleanup: `app/` and `web/` deleted, contract\r","+  extracted to `contract/`, `.gitignore` rewritten (`.env` was exposed),\r","+  `.workspace/` added, CI deleted — run `npm test --prefix contract` yourself.\r","+- **2026-11-07** · Henri · `DISCOVERY_SPEC.md` written from Jeremy's pitch.\r","+- **2026-11-07** · Jeremy · Discovery pipeline UI + Motus dashboard merged\r","+  (PRs #1, #2).\r","+\r","+---\r","+\r","+## If main gives you a `tsconfig.tsbuildinfo` conflict — read this first\r","+\r","+**Jeremy, this is the one you're hitting.** `frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo`\r","+is TypeScript's incremental build cache. It was committed by mistake, it\r","+rewrites itself on every single build, so it conflicted constantly. `main`\r","+untracked it on 2026-11-07 and it's gitignored now.\r","+\r","+Your branch has it modified, main deleted it → modify/delete conflict.\r","+Accept the deletion; it regenerates on your next build and will never come\r","+back:\r","+\r","+```bash\r","+git rm --cached frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo\r","+git commit --no-edit\r","+```\r","+\r","+One time only. Sorry — that one's on Henri, and it was the only file under\r","+`frontend/` that main touched.\r","+\r","+## Heads-up if you merge main\r","+\r","+`main` deleted `app/` on 2026-11-07, so branches that built there get\r","+modify/delete conflicts (measured: 11 on `cursor/pipeline-graph-ui`, 19 on\r","+`frontend/kg-and-provenance`). `Master-UI-Neo-Face-Integration` and\r","+`codex/diagnostic-tests` share **no common ancestor** with main and can't be\r","+merged without `--allow-unrelated-histories`. Your branch, your call."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\docs\\STATUS.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ecadfbf7-2cbb-4077-aed5-db9537946e8a","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/jerem/BioHacks-2026/frontend","root":"/c/Users/jerem/BioHacks-2026","branch":"frontend/diagnosis","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":3,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"penguinyogurt/BioHacks-2026","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"o