38.328Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\frontend","sessionId":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"frontend/diagnosis"}
{"parentUuid":"a815fe61-9753-4fcb-841f-0d0a1b986b5f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d6dd28df-5121-43fc-98ad-08951010d9c0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UDRJCBiXoaVhYN9u2HQm7L","type":"tool_result","content":"76:  (soma low on the left, axon rising to terminals upper right), name bottom-right; each\n\u001b[32m✓ built in 915ms\u001b[39m\n[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: ..\\docs\\STATUS.md. Call Read before editing.]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c8c3b4cf-2e05-49f3-9ad8-1031b452bf1d","timestamp":"2026-11-08T05:09:44.999Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"76:  (soma low on the left, axon rising to terminals upper right), name bottom-right; each\n\u001b[32m✓ built in 915ms\u001b[39m","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"staleReadFileStateHint":"[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: ..\\docs\\STATUS.md. Call Read before editing.]","bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\docs\\STATUS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":114,"newStart":1,"newLines":114,"lines":["-# Status — the shared task board\r","-\r","-**This is the one place work is claimed.** Read it at the start of every\r","-session. Claim before you write code. Release when you stop.\r","-\r","-There is no task framework to install — `gh` isn't on these machines and\r","-four people on three different AI harnesses have exactly one medium in\r","-common, which is this repo. So the board is a file, and the protocol below\r","-is what makes it work.\r","-\r","-Last updated: **2026-11-07**\r","-\r","----\r","-\r","-## How to claim (all of it)\r","-\r","-1. **`git pull`** — then put your name on the line you want, in **In flight**.\r","-2. **Commit just this file and push immediately.** Don't bundle the claim\r","-   with your work; the claim is worthless if it lands an hour later.\r","-   ```bash\r","-   git pull && git add docs/STATUS.md && git commit -m \"claim: <task>\" && git push\r","-   ```\r","-3. **If the push is rejected**, someone claimed something while you typed.\r","-   `git pull --rebase`, check your task is still free, push again.\r","-4. **When you stop** — done, blocked, or bored — move the line to **Done** or\r","-   back to **Open**, with one line on where you left it. A task parked\r","-   silently is the same as a task nobody did.\r","-\r","-If two of you end up on the same line anyway, that's a conflict in one\r","-markdown row. Keep both names, talk, move on.\r","-\r","-**Your task isn't on the board?** Most won't be. Add the line and claim it\r","-in the same push — that *is* the claim. Don't go looking for permission.\r","-\r","-**When not to claim.** Claiming costs a push, so it has to buy something.\r","-Skip it for anything another person could not plausibly start at the same\r","-time: reading code, answering a question, a typo, a one-line fix, anything\r","-under ~10 minutes. Claim when you're about to **create a file, change a\r","-shared one, or work somewhere for a while** — that's when collisions happen.\r","-A board full of \"fixed a typo\" is a board nobody reads.\r","-\r","----\r","-\r","-## In flight — claimed, don't touch\r","-\r","-| Who | Track | Branch | Task | Blocked on |\r","-|---|---|---|---|---|\r","-| Jeremy | discovery | `main` | FUS discovery pipeline — scripted end to end. See `DISCOVERY_SPEC.md` | A live backend behind `runDemoPipeline` |\r","-| Jeremy | frontend | `main` | Motus dashboard — overview landed, 15 views still placeholders | Supabase keys |\r","-| Neo | pipeline | `cursor/pipeline-graph-ui` | Drug pipeline — BBB + patient filter scored over 3,791 compounds | — |\r","-| Neo | facecheck | `cursor/facial-als-validation` | FaceCheck MediaPipe prototype | `FACECHECK_SPEC.md` §2 gaps |\r","-| Levi | speech | `Master-UI-Neo-Face-Integration` | Speech + diagnostic test apps | No spec in `docs/` yet |\r","-| Henri | repo | `main` | Cleanup, specs, this board | — |\r","-\r","-> Names are from git history. Fix them if they're wrong.\r","-\r","-## Open — unclaimed, grab one\r","-\r","-Ordered roughly by what hurts most if it's still open on Sunday morning.\r","-\r","-| Track | Task | Why it matters |\r","-|---|---|---|\r","-| **decision** | **Pick the product: discovery pipeline or Motus.** Both ship on `main`, in one sidebar, sharing nothing else | 90 seconds, one argument. Everything below depends on this |\r","-| **decision** | **Pick the name.** Code says *Addo Labs*, landing page says *motus* | A judge sees both in one scroll |\r","-| discovery | Wire the graveyard's `never_arrived` bucket in as the FUS candidate pool | It already exists in `data/pipeline.json` and is exactly the right set — `DISCOVERY_SPEC.md` §1 |\r","-| discovery | Real citations for the Sunnybrook MRgFUS claim; be precise about human vs proposed | The whole pitch rests on it, and someone will ask |\r","-| pipeline | Port the Python onto a branch cut from `main` (leave `data/*.json` and `artifacts/` behind) | `main` has no pipeline code today |\r","-| speech | Write `docs/SPEECH_SPEC.md` | The only track with no spec — nobody else can pick it up |\r","-| frontend | Decide demo mode: signed-in or sample data | Sample works today with no keys |\r","-| facecheck | Decide: own page, or a tab in the app | `FACECHECK_SPEC.md` §7 |\r","-| discovery | A real backend behind `runDemoPipeline` — stretch | The seam is clean; don't collapse it under time pressure |\r","-\r","-## Done\r","-\r","-- **2026-11-08** · Jeremy · Landing reworked: neuron lies horizontally, tilted\r","-  slightly (soma left, axon sloping down to the right), name bottom-right; each\r","-  action potential runs to the far terminals and an amber glow carries on down\r","-  to light the wordmark. Discovery pipeline now advances one stage per click, Gradient\r","-  ASCII background (React Bits, patched for StrictMode) replaces the dither.\r","-- **2026-11-07** · Henri · Repo cleanup: `app/` and `web/` deleted, contract\r","-  extracted to `contract/`, `.gitignore` rewritten (`.env` was exposed),\r","-  `.workspace/` added, CI deleted — run `npm test --prefix contract` yourself.\r","-- **2026-11-07** · Henri · `DISCOVERY_SPEC.md` written from Jeremy's pitch.\r","-- **2026-11-07** · Jeremy · Discovery pipeline UI + Motus dashboard merged\r","-  (PRs #1, #2).\r","-\r","----\r","-\r","-## If main gives you a `tsconfig.tsbuildinfo` conflict — read this first\r","-\r","-**Jeremy, this is the one you're hitting.** `frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo`\r","-is TypeScript's incremental build cache. It was committed by mistake, it\r","-rewrites itself on every single build, so it conflicted constantly. `main`\r","-untracked it on 2026-11-07 and it's gitignored now.\r","-\r","-Your branch has it modified, main deleted it → modify/delete conflict.\r","-Accept the deletion; it regenerates on your next build and will never come\r","-back:\r","-\r","-```bash\r","-git rm --cached frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo\r","-git commit --no-edit\r","-```\r","-\r","-One time only. Sorry — that one's on Henri, and it was the only file under\r","-`frontend/` that main touched.\r","-\r","-## Heads-up if you merge main\r","-\r","-`main` deleted `app/` on 2026-11-07, so branches that built there get\r","-modify/delete conflicts (measured: 11 on `cursor/pipeline-graph-ui`, 19 on\r","-`frontend/kg-and-provenance`). `Master-UI-Neo-Face-Integration` and\r","-`codex/diagnostic-tests` share **no common ancestor** with main and can't be\r","-merged without `--allow-unrelated-histories`. Your branch, your call.\r","+# Status — the shared task board","+","+**This is the one place work is claimed.** Read it at the start of every","+session. Claim before you write code. Release when you stop.","+","+There is no task framework to install — `gh` isn't on these machines and","+four people on three different AI harnesses have exactly one medium in","+common, which is this repo. So the board is a file, and the protocol below","+is what makes it work.","+","+Last updated: **2026-11-07**","+","+---","+","+## How to claim (all of it)","+","+1. **`git pull`** — then put your name on the line you want, in **In flight**.","+2. **Commit just this file and push immediately.** Don't bundle the claim","+   with your work; the claim is worthless if it lands an hour later.","+   ```bash","+   git pull && git add docs/STATUS.md && git commit -m \"claim: <task>\" && git push","+   ```","+3. **If the push is rejected**, someone claimed something while you typed.","+   `git pull --rebase`, check your task is still free, push again.","+4. **When you stop** — done, blocked, or bored — move the line to **Done** or","+   back to **Open**, with one line on where you left it. A task parked","+   silently is the same as a task nobody did.","+","+If two of you end up on the same line anyway, that's a conflict in one","+markdown row. Keep both names, talk, move on.","+","+**Your task isn't on the board?** Most won't be. Add the line and claim it","+in the same push — that *is* the claim. Don't go looking for permission.","+","+**When not to claim.** Claiming costs a push, so it has to buy something.","+Skip it for anything another person could not plausibly start at the same","+time: reading code, answering a question, a typo, a one-line fix, anything","+under ~10 minutes. Claim when you're about to **create a file, change a","+shared one, or work somewhere for a while** — that's when collisions happen.","+A board full of \"fixed a typo\" is a board nobody reads.","+","+---","+","+## In flight — claimed, don't touch","+","+| Who | Track | Branch | Task | Blocked on |","+|---|---|---|---|---|","+| Jeremy | discovery | `main` | FUS discovery pipeline — scripted end to end. See `DISCOVERY_SPEC.md` | A live backend behind `runDemoPipeline` |","+| Jeremy | frontend | `main` | Motus dashboard — overview landed, 15 views still placeholders | Supabase keys |","+| Neo | pipeline | `cursor/pipeline-graph-ui` | Drug pipeline — BBB + patient filter scored over 3,791 compounds | — |","+| Neo | facecheck | `cursor/facial-als-validation` | FaceCheck MediaPipe prototype | `FACECHECK_SPEC.md` §2 gaps |","+| Levi | speech | `Master-UI-Neo-Face-Integration` | Speech + diagnostic test apps | No spec in `docs/` yet |","+| Henri | repo | `main` | Cleanup, specs, this board | — |","+","+> Names are from git history. Fix them if they're wrong.","+","+## Open — unclaimed, grab one","+","+Ordered roughly by what hurts most if it's still open on Sunday morning.","+","+| Track | Task | Why it matters |","+|---|---|---|","+| **decision** | **Pick the product: discovery pipeline or Motus.** Both ship on `main`, in one sidebar, sharing nothing else | 90 seconds, one argument. Everything below depends on this |","+| **decision** | **Pick the name.** Code says *Addo Labs*, landing page says *motus* | A judge sees both in one scroll |","+| discovery | Wire the graveyard's `never_arrived` bucket in as the FUS candidate pool | It already exists in `data/pipeline.json` and is exactly the right set — `DISCOVERY_SPEC.md` §1 |","+| discovery | Real citations for the Sunnybrook MRgFUS claim; be precise about human vs proposed | The whole pitch rests on it, and someone will ask |","+| pipeline | Port the Python onto a branch cut from `main` (leave `data/*.json` and `artifacts/` behind) | `main` has no pipeline code today |","+| speech | Write `docs/SPEECH_SPEC.md` | The only track with no spec — nobody else can pick it up |","+| frontend | Decide demo mode: signed-in or sample data | Sample works today with no keys |","+| facecheck | Decide: own page, or a tab in the app | `FACECHECK_SPEC.md` §7 |","+| discovery | A real backend behind `runDemoPipeline` — stretch | The seam is clean; don't collapse it under time pressure |","+","+## Done","+","+- **2026-11-08** · Jeremy · Landing reworked: neuron lies horizontally, tilted","+  (soma low on the left, axon rising to terminals upper right), name bottom-right; each","+  action potential runs to the far terminals and an amber glow carries on down","+  to light the wordmark. Discovery pipeline now advances one stage per click, Gradient","+  ASCII background (React Bits, patched for StrictMode) replaces the dither.","+- **2026-11-07** · Henri · Repo cleanup: `app/` and `web/` deleted, contract","+  extracted to `contract/`, `.gitignore` rewritten (`.env` was exposed),","+  `.workspace/` added, CI deleted — run `npm test --prefix contract` yourself.","+- **2026-11-07** · Henri · `DISCOVERY_SPEC.md` written from Jeremy's pitch.","+- **2026-11-07** · Jeremy · Discovery pipeline UI + Motus dashboard merged","+  (PRs #1, #2).","+","+---","+","+## If main gives you a `tsconfig.tsbuildinfo` conflict — read this first","+","+**Jeremy, this is the one you're hitting.** `frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo`","+is TypeScript's incremental build cache. It was committed by mistake, it","+rewrites itself on every single build, so it conflicted constantly. `main`","+untracked it on 2026-11-07 and it's gitignored now.","+","+Your branch has it modified, main deleted it → modify/delete conflict.","+Accept the deletion; it regenerates on your next build and will never come","+back:","+","+```bash","+git rm --cached frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo","+git commit --no-edit","+```","+","+One time only. Sorry — that one's on Henri, and it was the only file under","+`frontend/` that main touched.","+","+## Heads-up if you merge main","+","+`main` deleted `app/` on 2026-11-07, so branches that built there get","+modify/delete conflicts (measured: 11 on `cursor/pipeline-graph-ui`, 19 on","+`frontend/kg-and-provenance`). `Master-UI-Neo-Face-Integration` and","+`codex/diagnostic-tests` share **no common ancestor** with main and can't be","+merged without `--allow-unrelated-histories`. Your branch, your call."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\docs\\STATUS.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"3288b9de-b2cf-430b-b132-4620302a741d