{"parentUuid":"55f70c50-5f1f-4ad3-87b4-aee61d72e43d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgpv9cCFbswKAfVxvTPkh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The tag says \"Simulated run\" (not \"stimulated\"), and it's only a label: it has no tooltip or hidden content. It appears in the header of every pipeline page (`StageHeader` in `src/components/discovery/pieces.tsx`).\n\nIt's there because the pipeline isn't connected to real agents yet. Clicking a run step replays a fixed script (`runDemoStage` in `src/lib/pipeline.ts`): the NCBI, ClinVar and DRKG calls in the traces, the five profiles, the cosine scores, the candidate ranking and the report are all written in advance. They're also the same regardless of which PDF you upload. The badge makes sure nobody mistakes those numbers for real output during the demo. The report carries a matching \"Simulated run · illustrative outputs\" badge.\n\nIf it's confusing, I can add a hover tooltip saying the outputs are scripted for the demo, reword it (e.g. \"Demo data\"), or remove it once a real backend is connected."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27,"cache_read_input_tokens":884170,"output_tokens":425,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":100},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":425,"cache_read_input_tokens":884170,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.98.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messag